Package: BayGMST
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Reconstruction of Global Mean Surface Temperature
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tyler", "Bagwell", email = "teb6@rice.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Julien", "Emile-Geay", email = "julieneg@usc.edu",
           role = "aut"))
Maintainer: Tyler Bagwell <teb6@rice.edu>
Description: Fits a Bayesian hierarchical AR(1) state-space model relating
    global mean surface temperature (GMST) to a reduced paleoclimate proxy
    network, instrumental temperature observations, and radiative forcings
    (greenhouse gases, volcanic aerosols, and solar irradiance). Missing
    pre-instrumental temperatures are estimated jointly with the model
    parameters using 'Stan' via the 'instantiate' and 'cmdstanr' packages.
    Includes tools to reduce a multi-proxy network to a single representative
    proxy series (via principal component regression, partial least squares,
    LASSO, or supervised PCR), fit the reconstruction model, run k-fold
    cross-validation, and visualize reconstructions and posterior draws.
    Implements the model described in Bagwell et al. (in prep).
